                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Initial length \\( L_0 = 20.0\\,\\mathrm{m} \\), \\( \\alpha = 1.1 \\times 10^{-5}\\,^\\circ\\mathrm{C}^{-1} \\), \\( \\Delta T = 100\\,^\\circ\\mathrm{C} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Final length \\( L \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( L = L_0(1 + \\alpha \\Delta T) \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> Direct calculation.<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( L = 20.0 \\times [1 + (1.1 \\times 10^{-5} \\times 100)] \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( \\alpha \\Delta T = 1.1 \\times 10^{-3} = 0.0011 \\); \\( 1 + 0.0011 = 1.0011 \\); \\( L = 20.0 \\times 1.0011 = 20.022\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 20.022\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> The pipe expands by 0.022 m (22 mm), so flexible expansion loops must be installed in steam heating pipes."
