                    options: ["5.0 C", "405 C", "0.20 C", "54 C"],
                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Voltage \\( V = 9.0\\,\\mathrm{V} \\), Energy / Work \\( W = 45.0\\,\\mathrm{J} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Charge \\( q \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( V = \\frac{W}{q} \\implies q = \\frac{W}{V} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( q = \\frac{W}{V} \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( q = \\frac{45.0\\,\\mathrm{J}}{9.0\\,\\mathrm{V}} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( \\frac{45.0}{9.0} = 5.0\\,\\mathrm{C} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 5.0\\,\\mathrm{C} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Dividing total work by voltage reveals the total Coulomb quantity of charge moved."
