                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> First leg \\( d_1 = 60\\,\\mathrm{km} \\) at \\( v_1 = 60\\,\\mathrm{km/h} \\); Second leg \\( d_2 = 60\\,\\mathrm{km} \\) at \\( v_2 = 30\\,\\mathrm{km/h} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Average speed \\( v_{\\text{avg}} \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( t_1 = \\frac{d_1}{v_1} \\), \\( t_2 = \\frac{d_2}{v_2} \\), \\( v_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{d_1 + d_2}{t_1 + t_2} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Quantities in consistent km and h.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> Calculate leg times before finding overall average.<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( t_1 = \\frac{60}{60} = 1.0\\,\\mathrm{h} \\); \\( t_2 = \\frac{60}{30} = 2.0\\,\\mathrm{h} \\); Total time = \\( 1.0 + 2.0 = 3.0\\,\\mathrm{h} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> Total distance = \\( 60 + 60 = 120\\,\\mathrm{km} \\); \\( v_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{120\\,\\mathrm{km}}{3.0\\,\\mathrm{h}} = 40\\,\\mathrm{km/h} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 40\\,\\mathrm{km/h} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> The car spends more time (2 h) traveling at the slower speed, weighting the average speed toward 30 km/h. (The arithmetic mean 45 km/h is incorrect!)."
