                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Initial velocity \\( u = 0 \\), Acceleration \\( a = 2.50\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\), Time \\( t = 8.00\\,\\mathrm{s} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Final velocity \\( v \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v = u + at \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Convert to km/h by multiplying by 3.6.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> Formula is solved for \\( v \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( v = 0 + (2.50 \\times 8.00) \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( v = 20.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\); In km/h: \\( 20.0 \\times 3.6 = 72.0\\,\\mathrm{km/h} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 20.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\) (72.0 km/h).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Under uniform acceleration from rest, velocity gained is the product of acceleration and time."
