                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Initial velocity \\( u = 25.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\), Final velocity \\( v = 0 \\), Deceleration \\( a = -5.00\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Stopping distance \\( s \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v^2 = u^2 + 2as \\implies s = \\frac{v^2 - u^2}{2a} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( s = \\frac{-u^2}{2a} \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( s = \\frac{0 - (25.0)^2}{2(-5.00)} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( 25.0^2 = 625 \\); \\( s = \\frac{-625}{-10.0} = 62.5\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 62.5\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> The fourth equation determines stopping distance directly without requiring elapsed time."
