                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Initial velocity \\( u = 0 \\), \\( g = 9.80\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\), Time \\( t = 4.00\\,\\mathrm{s} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Final velocity \\( v \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v = u + gt \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( v = gt \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( v = 9.80\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\times 4.00\\,\\mathrm{s} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( 9.80 \\times 4.00 = 39.2\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 39.2\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\) downwards.<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Under gravity, downward speed increases by 9.80 m/s during every second of unobstructed fall."
