                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Launch velocity \\( u = 28.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\), \\( g = 9.80\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\), \\( v = 0 \\) at apex.<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Maximum height \\( H_{\\max} \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v^2 = u^2 - 2gH_{\\max} \\implies H_{\\max} = \\frac{u^2}{2g} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( H_{\\max} = \\frac{u^2}{2g} \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( H_{\\max} = \\frac{(28.0)^2}{2(9.80)} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( 28.0^2 = 784 \\); \\( 2g = 19.6 \\); \\( H_{\\max} = \\frac{784}{19.6} = 40.0\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 40.0\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Kinetic energy at launch converts completely into gravitational potential energy at the peak."
