                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Peak height \\( H = 20.0\\,\\mathrm{m} \\), \\( g = 9.80\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\), \\( v = 0 \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Launch velocity \\( u \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v^2 = u^2 - 2gH \\implies u = \\sqrt{2gH} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( u = \\sqrt{2gH} \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( u = \\sqrt{2(9.80)(20.0)} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( 2 \\times 9.80 \\times 20.0 = 392 \\); \\( u = \\sqrt{392} \\approx 19.8\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 19.8\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Launch velocity required to reach a specific vertical height scales with \\( \\sqrt{2gH} \\)."
