                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Drop height \\( h = 108\\,\\mathrm{m} \\), \\( g = 9.80\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Speed \\( v \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( v = \\sqrt{2gh} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> Direct calculation.<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( v = \\sqrt{2 \\times 9.80 \\times 108} = \\sqrt{2116.8} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> \\( v \\approx 46.01\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\approx 46.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 46.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\) (166 km/h).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Gravitational descent converts potential energy into 46.0 m/s impact velocity."
