                    solution: "1. <strong>Weight in air:</strong> \\( 5.40 \\times 9.80 = 52.92\\,\\mathrm{N} \\).<br>2. <strong>Buoyant force:</strong> \\( 1000 \\times 9.80 \\times 0.00200 = 19.60\\,\\mathrm{N} \\).<br>3. <strong>Apparent submerged weight:</strong><br>\\[ W_{\\text{app}} = 52.92 - 19.60 = 33.32\\,\\mathrm{N} \\]",
                    finalAnswer: "W_{\\text{air}} = 52.92\\,\\mathrm{N}, \\quad F_B = 19.60\\,\\mathrm{N}, \\quad W_{\\text{app}} = 33.32\\,\\mathrm{N}",
                    explanation: "Submersion reduces the apparent weight by exactly the 19.6 N buoyant upthrust."
