                    correctIndex: 0,
                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> \\( l_1 = 0.10\\,\\mathrm{m} \\), \\( l_2 = 0.40\\,\\mathrm{m} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> \\( (A/V)_1 \\) and \\( (A/V)_2 \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( \\frac{A}{V} = \\frac{6}{l} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> Direct calculation.<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( (A/V)_1 = \\frac{6}{0.10} = 60\\,\\mathrm{m^{-1}} \\); \\( (A/V)_2 = \\frac{6}{0.40} = 15\\,\\mathrm{m^{-1}} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> Ratio: \\( \\frac{60}{15} = 4.0 \\).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> Small: 60 m⁻¹, Large: 15 m⁻¹ (Small cools 4 times faster).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> The small cube has 4 times more surface area per unit volume, radiating stored heat 4 times faster."
