                    feedback: "<strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br>1. <strong>Given:</strong> Distance \\( d = 1.50 \\times 10^{11}\\,\\mathrm{m} \\), Speed \\( c = 3.0 \\times 10^8\\,\\mathrm{m/s} \\).<br>2. <strong>Find:</strong> Time \\( t \\).<br>3. <strong>Equation:</strong> \\( t = \\frac{d}{c} \\).<br>4. <strong>Unit conversion:</strong> Standard SI units.<br>5. <strong>Rearrangement:</strong> \\( t = \\frac{1.50 \\times 10^{11}}{3.0 \\times 10^8} \\).<br>6. <strong>Substitution:</strong> \\( t = 500\\,\\mathrm{s} \\).<br>7. <strong>Calculation:</strong> In minutes: \\( \\frac{500}{60} = 8.33\\,\\text{minutes} \\) (8 min 20 s).<br>8. <strong>Final Answer:</strong> \\( 500\\,\\mathrm{s} \\) (approx. 8.33 minutes).<br>9. <strong>Explanation:</strong> Solar thermal radiation bridges the 150 million km vacuum in 8.33 minutes."
