                    solution: "1. <strong>Force from q₁ on q₂:</strong> Attracted towards q₁ (left, -x direction):<br>\\( F_{1 \\to 2} = \\frac{(9.0 \\times 10^9) \\times (2.0 \\times 10^{-6}) \\times (1.0 \\times 10^{-6})}{(0.10)^2} = \\frac{0.018}{0.010} = 1.80\\,\\mathrm{N} \\; (-\\hat{i}) \\).<br>2. <strong>Force from q₃ on q₂:</strong> Attracted towards q₃ (right, +x direction):<br>\\( F_{3 \\to 2} = \\frac{(9.0 \\times 10^9) \\times (1.0 \\times 10^{-6}) \\times (4.0 \\times 10^{-6})}{(0.20)^2} = \\frac{0.036}{0.040} = 0.90\\,\\mathrm{N} \\; (+\\hat{i}) \\).<br>3. <strong>Net force:</strong> \\( F_{\\text{net}} = +0.90 - 1.80 = -0.90\\,\\mathrm{N} \\).",
                    finalAnswer: "\\vec{F}_{2,\\text{net}} = 0.90\\,\\mathrm{N} \\text{ (Directed left towards } q_1\\text{)}",
