                    feedback: "1. Given: Particle undergoing SHM at central equilibrium position (x = 0).\n2. Find: Reason why a = 0 when |v| = v_max.\n3. Equation: F_net = -k·x = m·a ⟹ a(t) = -ω²·x(t).\n4. Unit conversion: None.\n5. Rearrangement: When x = 0, a = -ω²(0) = 0.\n6. Substitution: Energy conservation gives (1/2)mv² = (1/2)kA² - (1/2)kx²; when x = 0, v reaches v_max.\n7. Calculation: At x = 0, spring deformation is zero, so restoring force and acceleration are identically zero.\n8. Final Answer: Because restoring force depends on displacement (F = -kx), and at equilibrium x = 0, so net force and acceleration are zero.\n9. Short explanation: Acceleration in SHM is proportional to displacement; at the equilibrium midpoint, restoring force vanishes even as the particle hurtles through at maximum speed."
